      "Box meshes (8 vertices, or several disjoint 8-vertex boxes) become IR boxes. The non-box static meshes Bullet used are kept part by part: the B_01 storage box is 5 boxes; each B_03 gutter (a half-pipe profile extruded along the lane) becomes one 2 cm slab per profile segment, top face on the surface.",
      "B_01 floor becomes an infinite plane at its top face.",
      "B_03 pins (lathe meshes, convex hulls in Bullet) become cylinders r = 0.0605 m, h = 0.381 m, so their centre of mass sits higher (0.19 m vs about 0.14 m) and their base is wider.",
      "Materials: 4DCodeBench set Blender values, which Bullet multiplies per pair. The IR stores value**2, so bullet_blender (IR -> sqrt) reproduces the original pairs exactly; other engines combine pairs by their own rule (MuJoCo max, PhysX average, Newton XPBD average).",
      "Damping is 0 (the original used small plank / pin damping; Newton has no per-body damping).",
      "The ball is dynamic from frame 0 with the velocity of its scripted release track and rolling spin, instead of being animated for the first frames.",
      "Window, window pane and baseboards were excluded from the original Bullet world; same here."
